ia under  a tropical storm warning  emergency planners say losing hurricane  status  doesn't make teddy harmless i know  people are attracted to the shoreline  they love to watch the waves  i just want to caution folks please stay  back back at the yacht club they're  worried about what will happen when  winds  shift on wednesday during the expected  height of the storm  if we get a hit the that south west wind  at a high tide with a surge yeah we we  could experience some difficulties and  the  parking lot here will likely be uh  underwater we're going to be  uh in the top floor of their building in  sleeping bags  because uh it's not safe to be on a boat  in this kind of weather  by way of context hurricane juan in 2003  did 200 million dollars worth of damage  and is blamed for four deaths  hurricane dorian last year also left a  trail of devastation  forecasters say teddy is no one and no  dorian  but it could still be dangerous donna  ross lord on cape breton island tonight  thanks  we are going to keep tracking teddy's  path a little later our chief  meteorologist tells us where  exactly it is and when it will hit  britain's prime minister addressed the  nation tonight warning of a long winter  ahead  boris johnson is reimposing tough public  health restrictions because covid19 is  spreading again  there are almost 5 000 new positive  tests in 24 hours there the highest  daily numbers since early may  johnson who himself had coveted and  ended up in intensive care  chastised young people who don't seem to  care saying  your mild cough can be someone else's  death knell  crystal commansing reports we must take  action now because the stitching time  saves nine and this way  we can keep people in work we can keep  our shops and our schools open and we  can keep our country  moving forward a plea from the british  prime minister as  tough new restrictions come into effect  in pubs for example there's no more  standing only  table service is permitted and only  un